course: dictionary
lesson: 11261
title: Wrapper: the cover around a thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wrapper is the paper, foil or plastic that covers a sweet, a snack or a present. You can see the word in action here: «Keep a snack wrapper in your pocket or bag until you find a bin.» The wrapper is the empty packet that once held the snack.
explain: A wrapper can also be anything that covers or wraps something else. The words around the word help you. In «Ellie and her mum make a memory box for Grandad: his glasses, a photo, the wrapper from his favourite sweets», the list shows that the wrapper is a thing to keep, not something to throw away.
explain: Sometimes the word appears with another word in front of it, like «candy wrapper», «sweet wrapper» (UK) or «chocolate wrapper». The first word tells you what kind of thing is being covered. Ask yourself: what is inside? That is a quick way to work out the meaning.
fact: A wrapper is the paper, foil or plastic around a candy, a snack or a present.
fact: Wrapper can also mean anything that covers or wraps something else.
fact: Common phrases are «candy wrapper», «sweet wrapper» (UK) and «chocolate wrapper».
fact: Wrappers are litter, so put them in a bin or recycle them.
fact: In quiet places, rustling wrappers in a film can spoil things for other people.
exercise: «He felt sick eating them, and Dad found the wrappers in his pocket.» What were the wrappers? | Notes from school | A kind of pocket for coins | *The paper or plastic that covered the sweets | Tiny pieces of bread
exercise: «Keep a snack wrapper in your pocket or bag until you find a bin, because litter harms animals.» Why should you keep the wrapper? | Because wrappers are worth money | Because bins are always full | *Because litter harms animals and spoils places | Because wrappers can be eaten later
exercise: Find and copy the UK phrase for a sweet packet. | *sweet wrapper | chocolate tin | sweet box | candy bag
test: «And Grace's friend said "I didn't eat your sweets", then Grace found the wrapper in her bag.» What did the wrapper show? | That the bag was new | That Grace had won a prize | That the friend had lost her bag | *That the friend had eaten Grace's sweets
test: Why does the author list «the wrapper from his favourite sweets» in the memory box? | Because Grandad asked for litter | *Because it is a keepsake that reminds Ellie of Grandad | Because the box needed something heavy | Because wrappers are good for cleaning glasses
exam: What does wrapper mean? | A bin for litter | A sweet that is still inside its packet | *The paper, foil or plastic that covers a candy, snack or present | The shop where you buy snacks
